Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 13:21:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix common.json corruption (complete): remove remaining 102
 orphaned/dead top-level keys

Round 4 fix (9bd906b) only removed the explicitly-named blocks (otp, phone,
location, notification, welcome, interests, contacts, 5 corrupted keys) but
left ~82% of common.json (102 of 125 top-level keys) as dead duplicate content
from the same extraction bug -- content copy-pasted into common.json but
actually read from dedicated namespace files (profile/*.json, safety/*.json,
wallet/*.json, verify/*.json, home/discover.json, home/companionProfile.json,
settings/*.json, etc).

Verified via:
- grep of all useTranslation('common')/(['common'])/() call sites across the
  codebase (16 files), scoped per-component to exclude dead unused t vars in
  reusable subcomponents (CustomSwitch/CustomSlider patterns)
- cross-referenced each orphaned top-level key against every other locale
  namespace file to confirm duplicate content exists elsewhere with matching
  real values (97/102 confirmed duplicated; remaining 5 -- consent, discover,
  error, loading, retry -- confirmed to have zero t() call sites anywhere)

Only 23 top-level keys are genuinely read via the common namespace and are
kept: appName, chatInput, companionCard, 12 a11y* keys, stepCounter, and the
5 tab* keys used by MainTabNavigator.

Verification:
- python3 json.load() -> valid JSON
- npx tsc --noEmit -> 0 errors
- regression scan of all t() calls in common-namespace-using files -> 0 missing keys
